      "scope": "Grade 6–7; Concise block (80–250 words)",
      "blueprint": true,
      "blueprintProse": "The BAB framework balances its structure into three balanced sections: 35% dedicated to Before, 35% to After, and 30% to the Bridge. The Before section grounds the narrative in the reader's current reality, marked by manual toil and inefficiencies. The After section constructs an alternative reality where those operational burdens have been eradicated. The Bridge introduces the specific technology, methodology, or tool that connects the painful baseline to the frictionless outcome. \nThe cognitive foundation of BAB relies on perceptual contrast and counterfactual simulation. By establishing an explicit contrast between the baseline and the transformed state, the copy exploits the brain's anchoring tendencies. Counterfactual thinking creates cognitive dissonance between the user's current situation and their potential future, transforming the product into an indispensable conduit for progress.",
