      "scope": "Grade 8–9; Long-form narrative (500–2,000 words)",
      "blueprint": true,
      "blueprintProse": "The QUEST framework organizes long-form educational copy through five distinct communicative blocks. Qualify opens the copy with 15% of the total budget, identifying who the material is for while filtering out inappropriate prospects. Understand takes 20%, establishing empathy through granular articulation of the reader's operational bottlenecks. Educate forms the intellectual core with 30%, teaching an analytical model or exposing a structural industry misconception. Stimulate occupies 20%, detailing the quantitative leverage achieved when the educational principle is applied. Transition completes the final 15%, guiding the reader from conceptual agreement to commercial engagement. \nQUEST leverages framing theory and commitment consistency. By educating prospects and delivering objective insights before asking for capital, the author activates the reciprocity norm. The systematic qualification sequence also triggers in-group status validation: readers who match the qualification criteria feel compelled to maintain consistency with that high-value professional identity.",
