      "scope": "Grade 6–7; Alert banner (15–35 words)",
      "blueprint": true,
      "blueprintProse": "Blameless error messages divide their content into three balanced components: an objective status description (30%), a technical cause statement (30%), and an immediate remediation pathway (40%). \nThis approach is grounded in attribution theory and locus-of-control preservation. Accusatory error messages trigger frustration and defense mechanisms, often causing users to abandon the application. Framing errors as neutral system conditions paired with direct remediation links maintains user composure and workflow efficiency.",
